From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anaconda Recipes <recipes@anaconda.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Jul 2026 12:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Extend gcc SVE ICE workaround to gcc 15

Upstream commit 8fd50939 added __attribute__((optimize("no-tree-vectorize")))
on unfolded2d_acc_kernel to work around a gcc-14.2.0 ICE during RTL pass:
vregs when compiling for SVE. See pytorch/pytorch#172630.

The same ICE class re-appears with gcc 15.2.0 building for linux-aarch64
(-march=armv8-a+sve+bf16 -msve-vector-bits=256):

  Unfold2d.cpp:226:1: error: unrecognizable insn:
    (insn ... (set (reg:VNx8BI 2854) (unspec:VNx16BI [(reg:VNx8BI 2856) (nil)]))
  during RTL pass: vregs
  internal compiler error: in extract_insn, at recog.cc:2882

AR's ctng-compiler-activation ships gcc 15.2.0 for linux-aarch64 (14.3 has
a distinct vector-instruction bug). Extend the workaround gate from
__GNUC__ == 14 to __GNUC__ >= 14 so it also applies to gcc 15.

Once upstream widens the gate, or gcc 15.3+ ships the RTL fix, this
patch can be dropped.
---
diff --git a/aten/src/ATen/native/cpu/Unfold2d.cpp b/aten/src/ATen/native/cpu/Unfold2d.cpp
index 9ae1391e2..49ba11af2 100644
--- a/aten/src/ATen/native/cpu/Unfold2d.cpp
+++ b/aten/src/ATen/native/cpu/Unfold2d.cpp
@@ -169,7 +169,7 @@ void unfolded2d_acc_channels_last(
 
 /* note: due to write issues, this one cannot be parallelized as well as
  * unfolded2d_copy */
-#if defined(__GNUC__) && __GNUC__ == 14 && defined(__ARM_FEATURE_SVE)
+#if defined(__GNUC__) && __GNUC__ >= 14 && defined(__ARM_FEATURE_SVE)
 // Workaround for gcc-14.2.0 ICE during RTL pass: vregs when compiling for SVE
 // NS: With or without BF16, see https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/issues/172630
 __attribute__((optimize("no-tree-vectorize")))
-- 
2.42.0

